{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1098743-werewolfs-assaulting-a-vampire-controlled-city","id":1098743,"title":"Werewolfs \"assaulting\" a Vampire controlled city","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-31T06:33:18-07:00","id":1098743,"title":"Werewolfs \"assaulting\" a Vampire controlled city","content":"<br /> Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> I am writing a chronicle for VTM and I\u2019d like to get some inspiration from experienced Werewolf players.<br /> <br /> The chronicle is set in modern days Kaliningrad, the Russian exclave east of Poland.<br /> It is a Camarilla Domain and my group will consist of Neonate Camarilla members.<br /> <br /> I intent to present the city as Wyrm tainted.<br /> The people are dirty, poor, many are drug consumers. Violence is omnipresent on the streets.<br /> Economic outlook is generally bad and the city administration runs mainly through bribes.<br /> Some PENTEX subsidiaries are also present and increase the local Wyrm corruption.<br /> The vampires have a very high influence in almost all business and admistrativ branches.<br /> <br /> The main antagonist of the chronicle should be two or three packs of Garou which repopulate a deserted Cearn outside of the City.<br /> I would assume that they will consist largely of a mix of Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords due to the geographical region.<br /> <br /> Now here is my question. They Garou will notice that the city is tainted and that vampires are very influential there and they want to cleanse it<br /> and get rid of the vampiric influence. How will they do that. What is an appropriate \u201cattack\u201d strategy for the Garou to cleanse a city?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want to present a killing spree with one dead kindred every night rather a long term substile struggle for the power in the City.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your inspiration.<ul><li>No native speaker. Sorry for any mistakes-</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13526-duktusray","name":"DuktusRay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T07:15:08-07:00","id":1098754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DuktusRay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1098743-werewolfs-assaulting-a-vampire-controlled-city#post1098743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone,<br /> <br /> I am writing a chronicle for VTM and I\u2019d like to get some inspiration from experienced Werewolf players.<br /> <br /> The chronicle is set in modern days Kaliningrad, the Russian exclave east of Poland.<br /> It is a Camarilla Domain and my group will consist of Neonate Camarilla members.<br /> <br /> I intent to present the city as Wyrm tainted.</div> </div> </div> </div>That pretty much is going to go without saying. Cities in the WoD are like looming, gothic-style castles of evil that are larger than they are in the real world. Corruption is rampant all over, in both a spiritual and civil sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The people are dirty, poor, many are drug consumers. Violence is omnipresent on the streets.<br /> Economic outlook is generally bad and the city administration runs mainly through bribes.<br /> Some PENTEX subsidiaries are also present and increase the local Wyrm corruption.<br /> The vampires have a very high influence in almost all business and admistrativ branches. </div> </div> </div>Again, that doesn't really distinguish it from any other city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The main antagonist of the chronicle should be two or three packs of Garou which repopulate a deserted Cearn outside of the City.<br /> I would assume that they will consist largely of a mix of Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords due to the geographical region.<br /> <br /> Now here is my question. They Garou will notice that the city is tainted and that vampires are very influential there and they want to cleanse it<br /> and get rid of the vampiric influence. How will they do that. What is an appropriate \u201cattack\u201d strategy for the Garou to cleanse a city? </div> </div> </div>Garou don't necessarily usually try to do it, so there isn't a typical one. Also important to note, Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers are more common in cities than any other tribes regardless of region, and Russia plays host to all of the tribes but the Fianna. The ones who are already going to have plans to deal with the vampires are most likely the Glass Walkers; the Shadow Lords can step in to try and help in places and at times. The Silver Fangs most likely to interact with human politics, though, are among the Lodge of the Sun, so they might advocate taking a more hands-on approach to dealing with vampires, given their spiritual correspondence.<br /> <br /> In general, most of the efforts are also going to be things that make vampires scratch their heads in confusion. They will be indirect in a way that vampires just don't get, because they don't know about spirits. Everything they do short of just outright killing vampires or ousting Pentex subsidiaries will be a damned mystery.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don\u2019t want to present a killing spree with one dead kindred every night rather a long term substile struggle for the power in the City.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your inspiration.[*]No native speaker. Sorry for any mistakes- </div> </div> </div>No guarantees that you won't even with a subtle struggle! The Shadow Lords are just going to try and pin it on other vampires. Given some of their Gifts for getting people to do what they want, it might actually be another vampire that killed said vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T08:01:56-07:00","id":1098766,"title":"","content":"Kaliningrad is a Russian enclave surrounded by the EU (one of the thoughts on current Russian military actions is that Putin wants a land bridge to Kalingrad). A German city, it came into Russian possession during the end of World War II, and its importance to Russia increased dramatically after the collapse of the USSR. It is an old city, founded during the 13th century by the Teutonic Knights, so it would have likely been the base of Ventrue operations against the Tzimisce of the Baltics.<br /> <br /> Kaliningrad works as a cloak-and-dagger setting because it was once one of the largest military bases in the world (and still houses the Russian Baltic Fleet). If I remember correctly, Kalingrad possessed one of the Soviet nuclear waste reprocessing centers that supplied the tritium that the Soviets needed to maintain their thermonuclear weapons (it may still be operational for all that I know, allowing the Russians to maintain their failing thermonuclear arsenal). Since pollution from Kalingrad does not directly impact the rest of the Russian Federation, I would play up its role as a place where Russia sends stuff that it considers too dangerous for Siberia (if something goes wrong, it will effect Russia's rivals). It could also be a place where Russian laboratories are resurrecting the old Soviet experiments with Fomori soldiers, allowing the Russian military to gain access to 'special forces' with inhuman capabilities.<br /> <br /> Since you are designing it as a Camarilla city, it would likely be under the control of the Brujah, though the Ventrue would have likely made a push for it after the collapse of the Soviet Union. It would probably have a very high density of Kindred (1:5,000 would not be unreasonable), as the highly transient population of the military and the close proximity of the EU would allow less discrete Kindred to survive through 'hunting' expeditions into the EU. While the majority of the Kindred would be nominally Camarilla, I would expect a very large Tzmisce population that exist outside of the city proper. The Garou would likely come into conflict with the Kindred when they were tracking 'hunting parties' or when they were investigating the Russian laboratories that were creating Fomori soldiers. With a population of over 180 Kindred, the Garou would probably quickly kill off a dozen Kindred before they realize that the Kindred population of Kaliningrad is large enough to be a legitimate threat to their sept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T01:37:30-07:00","id":1099066,"title":"","content":"An important part to understand is both the Camarilla claims all Kindred AND can be very much a confederation of cities vs a single united organization. There are some high level functions but for the most part as long as they stick to the Traditions Princes vary on who or what can settle in their domain and count as citizens. One could Easily have an old clan Koldun claiming primogency, with his small brood in the city sure they might be some of the only cam tzim on the planet but each city is unique. Koldunism would allow a greater defense against &quot;Spirits solve all the problems for the Garou fighting vampires because they are basically blind&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}